  "result": "Perfect! \u2705 All 463 tests pass (447 existing + 16 new bulk discount tests).\n\n**Bulk discount feature implemented in `src/totals.js`:**\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Lines with qty \u2265 10 get an extra 2.5% discount\n- Applied AFTER the line's own (or tier) discount\n- Applied to the amount remaining after the first discount\n- Included in the `discount` field of `invoiceTotals`\n- VAT calculated on amount after both discounts\n\n**Example calculation (qty=10, no initial discount, 21% VAT):**\n- Line total: qty \u00d7 unitPrice = 10 \u00d7 1000 = 10,000\n- First discount: 0 (standard tier or no explicit discount)\n- Bulk discount: 10,000 \u00d7 2.5% = 250\n- Amount for VAT: 10,000 - 250 = 9,750\n- VAT: 9,750 \u00d7 21% = 2,047\n- Total: 10,000 - 250 + 2,047\n\n**Example with tiered discount (qty=10, 5% tier discount, 21% VAT):**\n- Line total: 10 \u00d7 1000 = 10,000\n- First discount: 10,000 \u00d7 5% = 500\n- Bulk discount: (10,000 - 500) \u00d7 2.5% = 237\n- Total discount: 500 + 237 = 737\n- Amount for VAT: 10,000 - 737 = 9,263\n- VAT: 9,263 \u00d7 21% = 1,945\n\n**Test coverage (16 new bulk discount tests):**\n- Threshold verification (qty=9 no bulk, qty=10 yes bulk)\n- Applied after tier discount\n- Applied after explicit line discount\n- Only on lines with qty \u2265 10\n- VAT calculated on correct amount\n- Multiple lines with mixed discounts\n- Large orders\n- Integration with vouchers\n- Mixed qty scenarios\n\nAll existing tests updated to account for bulk discount on qty \u2265 10 lines.",
